ulu\n1\nPrev Next\nAssessor\nSub Menu\nRelated Pages\nAbatement of Valuation or Taxes\nAssessor Services\nResources\nUpcoming Events/Meetings\nFull calendar\nHome\nDepartments\nAssessor\nMonday - Friday\n8 am - 4:30 pm\n507-765-3868\nfax: 507-765-2803\nQuestions: email\nPlease allow 2 business days for a response. |\n|\nRyan Rasmusson\nFillmore County Interim Assessor\n101 Fillmore Street, P.O. Box 466\nPreston, MN 55965 |\n|\nProperty Appraisers\nRyan Welscher\nAndy Hillery\nStefan Holets\nIsaak Solum |\n|\n|\nThe Fillmore County Assessor's Department is responsible for the valuation and classification of all real and taxable personal property within Fillmore County for property tax purposes as provided by the Minnesota State Statute. The Assessor's office also maintains property record data on all parcels.\n2026 Board of Appeal and Equalization Information\nFillmore County Public GIS Website Access (Beacon)\nNEW: Online Plat Search\nQuick Links\n2C Managed Forest Land\nGreen Acres/Rural Preserve\nUnderstanding The Appeals Process\nWhy Property Taxes Vary From Year to Year\nFillmore County Policy for Abatement of Valuation or Taxes\nShare this page\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.co.fillmore.mn.us/departments/land_records_assessor/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nEmployee Resources\nCounty Email\nIntranet\nTimekeeping System\nVPN\nContact\n101 Fillmore Street\nPreston, MN 55965\nDirectory\nAbout Us\nFillmore County is located on the southern border of Minnesota. Named for Millard Fillmore, the 13th President of the United States, our community is both agricultural and historic.\nFillmore County Mission Statement: Fillmore County's mission is to provide quality services to its citizens in an efficient, cost-effective manner.\n© 2026 Fillmore CO | Powered by revize , The Government Website Experts |\nLogin\nundefined\nundefined\nund